  "description": "At Reid, sustainability is at the heart of everything we do. We are committed to providing an environmentally friendly method of transport at an accessible price point, and the KADe truly embodies that mantra. For every product we sell, we plant a tree, and we aim to plant the seed of sustainable transport for generations to come.\nThe KADe II is the natural evolution of our KADe taking the platform to being a truly class leading product. The design maximizes load-carrying capacity while maintaining a smooth and controlled ride. We chose 24” wheels paired with reinforced 3.0” tires to improve ride quality and grip while keeping the center of gravity low.\nThe new ultra-low step through monocoque frame increases rigidity and structural integrity of the bike whilst reducing weight. Retaining the relaxed seat tube angle paired with a fully adjustable stem accommodates a wide range of rider heights, fitting riders between 5’4” and 6’4”. The KADe II now features internal cable routing to reduce maintenance and damage and comes equipped with upgraded dual 48v batteries with a combined 30ah storage (a huge 1440 watt hours!). These power the mid-drive Ananda M100 motor, boasting an impressive 110nm of torque—enough power to move any load and keep it moving for hours!\nThe KADe's versatility is unmatched, with a maximum load capacity of 100kg on the rear rack and 20kg on the front*. It includes built-in automatic front and rear lights and offers plenty of accessories. Whether it’s the school run, the weekly shop, a trip to the beach, or even using the KADe as a delivery vehicle, it can handle it all. With the extra demand of cargo, we have upgraded the bike’s components to meet these needs, featuring a Shimano CUES groupset and four-pot Tektro hydraulic disc brakes for reliable performance.\nOur team and their families love the KADe, and we are confident you will too. The KADe comes complete with mudguards, a rear carrier rack, and a front rack, with additional add-ons available to customize your ride.",
